      "source_id": "deeaaca6-7ec8-4a05-bbf4-2b22de70b024",
      "text": "It sounds like the soil is holding a lot of moisture right now, which is common with plastic pots. If you're worried about overwatering, try to monitor the soil moisture before watering them again—maybe just a gentle touch or a quick \"squeeze test\" on the top inch or so of soil to see if it still feels slightly damp. Better to be a bit on the light side than to have roots get waterlogged, which can cause rot!"
