      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s3",
      "source_id": "f6507f5a-e017-479e-8b80-3113d6e30786",
      "text": "Sounds like a smart approach! Monitoring the soil moisture directly is a good idea. Just remember to check the top layer first—if it still feels dry, that's your cue to water. Good luck with the monitoring! Let me know how it goes!"
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "0b6eae97-50fc-4d6e-90f0-a459cfd20cb5",
      "text": "That's exactly what I was thinking—checking the top layer first makes the most sense. I just hope I don't forget to do it when I'm distracted by the heat."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "f78f3ceb-a612-4be7-815b-3c39afe3f70b",
      "text": "No problem at all! Sometimes when things are hot, it’s easy to get distracted by the heat or the day’s schedule. Just try to set a quick reminder on your phone to check those pots twice a day. It should help keep you on track! Hope the heat doesn't cause too much stress for your plants!"
    }
  ]
